⟦shared:0⟧ returns unfiltered matches and cleavage coordinates;
⟦shared:1⟧ selects a display set. Enzyme site counts refer to
the full supplied sequence and remain stable after filtering. ⟦shared:2⟧ uses audited context only for exactly recognized bundled references;
it does not claim unknown samples are unblocked. This example explicitly uses ⟦shared:3⟧; this is a search assumption, not a measurement
of methylation in a physical sample. ⟦shared:4⟧ is the default route.
